// Plan stage R0z Z9c-B (part 1, R-VMOVE): `g` is a `once` closure, and each
// call of `f` spawns it. The second call runs it again (W0502). `f` moves
// `g` into itself (`ByMove`), so the call keeps the rule of main.
fn take(v: Vec<u64>) { print(v.len()) }
fn main() / async {
    let v = Vec.new()
    v.push(1)
    let g = || take(v)
    let f = || scope { s => s.spawn(g); () }
    f()
    f()
}
